  "term": "psychedelic drug",
  "definition": "A psychedelic drug is a substance studied in psychology for its links with altered mental experience, especially a stronger sense of connection to the self, other people, and the world. Research described in the packet also associates psychedelic drug use with changes in wellbeing and cognitive functions such as creativity.",
